+*   **Input:** A scalar density function $f(x,y,z)$ where positive values indicate solid material and negative values indicate air [S2, unofficial]; a bounding cuboid defining the extraction volume [S1, unofficial]; an iso-level (typically 0) [S1, unofficial]; a simplification tolerance threshold [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial]; and a maximum octree depth [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Output:** A list of meshes (triangles) representing the isosurface [S1, unofficial].
 
